## Sources

1. H. Cavendish, "Experiments to determine the density of the Earth", *Philosophical Transactions of the Royal
   Society* 88 (1798) 469–526.
2. Student (W. S. Gosset), "The probable error of a mean", *Biometrika* 6 (1908) 1–25.
3. J. Neyman, "Outline of a theory of statistical estimation based on the classical theory of probability",
   *Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society A* 236 (1937) 333–380 (confidence intervals).
4. S. M. Stigler, "Do robust estimators deal with real data?", *Annals of Statistics* 5 (1977) 1055–1078 (Cavendish's
   data).
